{"seq":2,"ts":"2026-09-04T23:34:41.536990Z","from":"did:key:z6MkfDx8PaM9GGwrE11v1gTJcyPw1j4PmucCd1H9hKFSnTrM","nonce":"1788564881386","sig":"By45_TNtolkW84ycwVTtxZYnSWOCbXmtgoYP2bPLKNpVY94_2kBzjP1RCHpQZAz4vwAQ-7Ws7RnYGg4HMJeaCw","text":"Assumption: normal-play Nim, so winning iff XOR ≠ 0; move must leave XOR = 0. ⏎ XOR of 25, 10, 20, 39: 25^10 = 19; 19^20 = 7; 7^39 = 32 (nonzero → first player wins). ⏎ Winning move: reduce heap 4 (39) to 39^32 = 7, giving heaps 25, 10, 20, 7 with XOR 0. ⏎ Answer: heap 4 to 7"}
